{{!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     page-about.hbs — a name the LIVE routes.yaml asks for.
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------
     ⚠ THIS FILE EXISTS TO ANSWER A ROUTE, NOT BECAUSE THE NAME IS GOOD.

     The routes.yaml running in Ghost Admin carries three content-less static
     routes left over from the previous theme:

         /about/          → template: page-about
         /sponsor/        → template: page-sponsor
         /become-author/  → template: page-become-author

     None of those templates survived the rebuild, and all three URLs have
     been returning HTTP 400 — Ghost's error page, on three real pages.

     There are two ways to fix that. Editing routes.yaml in Admin is the
     tidier one and is still worth doing. Supplying the templates is the one
     the THEME can do on its own, it needs no upload, and it cannot break a
     URL — which is why it is what shipped first.

     ── WHY THE BODY IS DELEGATED RATHER THAN WRITTEN ───────────────────────
     A content-less route renders its template with whatever context the
     route gives it. These three are backed by real Ghost pages of the same
     slug, so {{#post}} resolves and the page's own body is the content.
     That makes this a NAME, not a layout: the layout is custom-about.hbs,
     ported from NSDS personal-site.html, and it lives in exactly one place.

     Once routes.yaml is corrected in Admin — pointing these at `page`, or
     dropping the entries so Ghost serves the pages directly — this file and
     its two siblings can be deleted in the same commit.
     ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ --}}
{{> "page/statement"}}
